Z||000000||rodmcneill||10-11-2001||10:40 PM||||I came home early today from work and found my back door to the kitchen twisted and showing light. Whoever it was, had done a single kick to it and split the wood at the lower hinge. The door trim inside had also been popped off, at least they did not get in. The police came out a took a picture of it,a perfect footprint on the lower part of the door. My bicycle store was broken into  1 month ago and about $5000.00 merchandise stolen. I hate lowlife thieves.||||reg||8
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-11-2001||11:04 PM||||I know there are a lot of people who would always think about the criminals as a victim (and often they are, I've seen people turn to crime as a way of dealing with severe problems at home, etc)<P>but anyway.. I wish I had an electric fence around my home... not a regular cattle one, I mean a nice wrought iron one.. that just happened to be electrified..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'd rather have that than a gun in my home. (assuming I was allowed, which of course in Canada I'm not. not any gun I want anyway.. uzi's are cool. hehe.. but I've never even fired a pellet gun, so it doesn't matter anyway)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||6
