Z||000003||LarryB||10-11-2001||11:44 PM||||The problem with a gun is that if you're going to have and draw it you'd better be absolutely sure you're willing and able to use it without wavering or hesitating.  You don't want to end up becoming a different kind of victim.<P>Some states down here take a very dim view of homeowners shooting intruders, even at night, unless you can demonstrate that you reasonably believed your life was in immediate danger and you didn't have reasonable opportunity to escape.<P><p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||10-12-2001||12:28 AM||||Yeah, give me nice unstable loaded pet over a firearm any day. Say, a Kimodo Dragon, a Gila Monster, Green Mamba, or white bunny ('orrible fangs!)<P>Thing is, though, how would a gun help in a situation where you aren't at home? That's when the breakins happen... ||||reg||10
