Z||000012||fiero56||10-13-2001||08:08 PM||||When I was living in Columbus going to college there, we were living just a mile or two south of Obetz(must be the nastiest town in the nastiest city I have ever been to). One night my roomates and I heard people at our backdoor. By the time we chose our weapons of choice(me=really big pipe wrench, tony=baseball bat, matt=really thick wooden dowel rod)the guys at our door were gone. We left our weapons near the back door for the next occurrence. I think there wereabout 3 times people were at our door. We would have weapons in hand, and chase those mofos until they ran accross the highway on foot. We gave up once we hit the highway. Never did get a chance to wail on anyone, but given the opportunity, I have no doubt we would have.<P>I am waiting for the days when Ohio will allow concealed carry. I doubt I ever would, but I would want to be licensed, and it would be nice to know I could if I wanted, rather than have no choice. I've grown up around guns. My dad wanted his children to understand and respect guns, so all of us were exposed to them from very young until present. I still target practice on my grandparents land most everytime I head up to Michigan.||||reg||1
